      "notes": "Arduino alias: D0 / 16. Deep-sleep wake: connect D0 to RST so GPIO16 can pull RST LOW on wake (the board leaves R10 unfitted). No interrupts (Arduino core); only an internal pull-DOWN, no pull-up (INPUT_PULLDOWN_16). The official NodeMCU pin map says: GPIO read/write only, no interrupt, PWM, I2C or OneWire. The Arduino core does allow software PWM on pins 0-16. Board blue LED (LED1) is on this pin.",
      "verified": true
    },
